{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_012oPzWMnzu3DhkAGbmYLyBs", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://wiki.krisyotam.com/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic_2026-03/Harees\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zanzibar\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_sultans_of_Zanzibar\"}, {\"url\": \"https://pronounce.namedrop.io/how-to-pronounce-zanzibar/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://graphsearch.epfl.ch/en/concept/34414\"}, {\"url\": \"https://collections.tepapa.govt.nz/place/2001757\"}, {\"url\": \"https://nameberry.com/babyname/Zanzibar\"}, {\"url\": \"https://reflex.cnrs.fr/Lexiques/webball/biblio_bas.php?id=11907\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.originaltravel.co.uk/travel-blog/tanzania-and-zanzibar-beaches\"}, {\"url\": \"https://bibliotecavirtual.defensa.gob.es/BVMDefensa/pacifico/en/consulta_aut/registro.do?id=432192\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:33:50.256Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Harees Zanzibar name Wikipedia \"Zanzibar\" harees known as", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_018ehPjk28atBz8MoxCFPQ26", "content": [{"title": "wiki.krisyotam.com", "url": "https://wiki.krisyotam.com/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic_2026-03/Harees"}, {"title": "Zanzibar", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zanzibar"}, {"title": "List of sultans of Zanzibar", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_sultans_of_Zanzibar"}, {"title": "how to pronounce zanzibar", "url": "https://pronounce.namedrop.io/how-to-pronounce-zanzibar/"}, {"title": "graphsearch.epfl.ch", "url": "https://graphsearch.epfl.ch/en/concept/34414"}, {"title": "Free museum entry for New Zealanders and people living in New Zealand", "url": "https://collections.tepapa.govt.nz/place/2001757"}, {"title": "nameberry.com", "url": "https://nameberry.com/babyname/Zanzibar"}, {"title": "WEBBALL : n° 11907,", "url": "https://reflex.cnrs.fr/Lexiques/webball/biblio_bas.php?id=11907"}, {"title": "tanzania and zanzibar beaches", "url": "https://www.originaltravel.co.uk/travel-blog/tanzania-and-zanzibar-beaches"}, {"title": "bibliotecavirtual.defensa.gob.es", "url": "https://bibliotecavirtual.defensa.gob.es/BVMDefensa/pacifico/en/consulta_aut/registro.do?id=432192"}]}, "The search didn't find any source saying that harees is called \"Zanzibar\" or that the dish takes its name from the island. It returned two separate topics.\n\n**Harees itself:** A Wikipedia-derived page lists its alternative names as Hareesa, haleem, arizah, harisa, and jarish. It describes the dish as a dish of boiled, cracked, or coarsely-ground cracked wheat or bulgur, mixed with meat and seasoned. The name's etymology is traced to the Arabic verb for mashing or squashing grain (harasa).\n\n**Zanzibar's name:** Several sources trace the island's name to Persian and Arabic. One says the word Zanzibar came from Arabic zanjibār, which is in turn from Persian zangbâr, a compound of Zang (\"black\") + bâr (\"coast\"). Another, from a travel blog, offers a folk etymology involving Omani sailors, which it calls less plausible than the \"land of the black people\" reading.\n\nIf you were looking for a link between harees and Zanzibar, such as a Zanzibari version of the dish, the search results don't confirm one. A more targeted query, such as \"harees Zanzibar cuisine,\" might help."], "durationSeconds": 6.4454917499999995, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_012oPzWMnzu3DhkAGbmYLyBs", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
