{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01NMFPTdHyW3szhFbTZQa1a3", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.aljazeera.com/programmes/general/2009/01/200916101448660804.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.aljazeera.com/amp/video/2009/1/6/street-food-zanzibar\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hellskitchen.206.189.43.227.sslip.io/dish/3625\"}, {\"url\": \"https://standardmedia.co.ke/amp/-1'%20OR%203*2%3C(0%205%20597-597)%20--%20/article/2001500896/kenya-ismaili-imamat-sign-mou-on-climate-health-and-education\"}, {\"url\": \"https://standardmedia.co.ke/food/article/2001500896/easy-recipe-swahili-boko-boko-delight\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.standardmedia.co.ke/evewoman/living/article/2001500896/easy-recipe-swahili-boko-boko-delight\"}, {\"url\": \"https://standardmedia.co.ke/evewoman/food/article/2001500896/easy-recipe-swahili-boko-boko-delight\"}, {\"url\": \"https://standardmedia.co.ke/national/article/2001500896/kenya-ismaili-imamat-sign-mou-on-climate-health-and-education\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.arrivalguides.com/en/Travelguide/ZANZIBAR/dining/al-jabry-126700\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:33:58.790Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Zanzibar \"Boko Boko\" harees", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01L2tf6z12Mbdeh81L4jLw8Y", "content": [{"title": "www.aljazeera.com", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/programmes/general/2009/01/200916101448660804.html"}, {"title": "Street Food – Zanzibar", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/amp/video/2009/1/6/street-food-zanzibar"}, {"title": "Boko Boko Harees", "url": "https://hellskitchen.206.189.43.227.sslip.io/dish/3625"}, {"title": "Swahili Boko Boko delight (Photo: iStock)", "url": "https://standardmedia.co.ke/amp/-1'%20OR%203*2%3C(0%205%20597-597)%20--%20/article/2001500896/kenya-ismaili-imamat-sign-mou-on-climate-health-and-education"}, {"title": "easy recipe swahili boko boko delight", "url": "https://standardmedia.co.ke/food/article/2001500896/easy-recipe-swahili-boko-boko-delight"}, {"title": "easy recipe swahili boko boko delight", "url": "https://www.standardmedia.co.ke/evewoman/living/article/2001500896/easy-recipe-swahili-boko-boko-delight"}, {"title": "easy recipe swahili boko boko delight", "url": "https://standardmedia.co.ke/evewoman/food/article/2001500896/easy-recipe-swahili-boko-boko-delight"}, {"title": "kenya ismaili imamat sign mou on climate health and education", "url": "https://standardmedia.co.ke/national/article/2001500896/kenya-ismaili-imamat-sign-mou-on-climate-health-and-education"}, {"title": "al jabry 126700", "url": "https://www.arrivalguides.com/en/Travelguide/ZANZIBAR/dining/al-jabry-126700"}]}, "Searching for \"Zanzibar Boko Boko harees\" turned up a few relevant results, though none focuses specifically on Zanzibar's version.\n\n- **Zanzibar cuisine:** Al Jazeera's street food feature names bokoboko as a signature local dish whose character reflects the island's spice-trade past and later tourism. Al-Jabry in Zanzibar Town is described as the best place to try boko-boko, a meat porridge soup, usually made with beef.\n- **Name and origin:** A Kenyan Standard recipe says the dish is known as harees in the Middle East, and that Middle Eastern settlers brought it down to the East African coast. Its method is pounding cracked wheat with meat and rice, plus cinnamon, cardamom, and ghee.\n- **Harees link:** A recipe site describes boko boko as a Burundian variant of Arab harees, a wheat porridge made for Ramadan and Eid, and says Yemeni and Omani traders carried it along the Indian Ocean coast. This source looks less authoritative than the others, so treat it with caution.\n\nOverall, the sources agree that boko boko is a coastal East African dish tied to Arab harees and Omani/Yemeni trade. The results don't describe Zanzibar's preparation in detail."], "durationSeconds": 6.462803583000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01NMFPTdHyW3szhFbTZQa1a3", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgDVkHs7a2cXSw8GxwH72", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "In Zanzibar, harees is called **boko boko**, also spelled \"bokoboko\". It's a meat and cracked-wheat porridge, usually made with beef.\n\nSupport for this is mixed. The Kenyan Standard recipe says the dish is known as harees in the Middle East and that Middle Eastern settlers brought it to the East African coast. Al Jazeera's street-food feature names bokoboko as a signature Zanzibar dish. The Arrival Guides listing for Al-Jabry in Zanzibar Town describes boko-boko as a meat porridge soup. None of these sources states outright that boko boko is Zanzibar's name for harees, so that link is my inference from them. I didn't open the Wikipedia article on Harees itself, so I can't say whether it gives this name.\n\nSources:\n- [Easy recipe: Swahili boko boko delight (The Standard, Kenya)](https://standardmedia.co.ke/food/article/2001500896/easy-recipe-swahili-boko-boko-delight)\n- [Street Food – Zanzibar (Al Jazeera)](https://www.aljazeera.com/amp/video/2009/1/6/street-food-zanzibar)\n- [Al-Jabry, Zanzibar (Arrival Guides)](https://www.arrivalguides.com/en/Travelguide/ZANZIBAR/dining/al-jabry-126700)\n- [Harees (Wikipedia)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harees)"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1222, "cache_read_input_tokens": 6705, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1222}, "output_tokens": 501, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:34:05.345Z", "request_id": "req_011CgDVkHcUgEexX8khW8L4n"}
